\p \v 17 \w So Ruth gathered grain|strong="H03950"\w* \w in the field|strong="H07704"\w* \w until|strong="H05704"\w* \w evening|strong="H06153"\w*. \w And when she beat out|strong="H02251"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w what|strong="H00834"\w* \w she had gleaned|strong="H03950"\w*, \w it was|strong="H01961"\w* \w about an ephah|strong="H00374"\w* \w of barley|strong="H08184"\w*.\f + \fr 2:17 \fqa An ephah \ft is approximately 20 dry quarts or 22 liters (probably about 29 pounds or 13.2 kilograms of barley).\f* \v 18 \w She picked up the grain|strong="H05375"\w* \w and went into|strong="H00935"\w* \w the town|strong="H05892"\w*, \w where her mother-in-law|strong="H02545"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w saw|strong="H07200"\w* \w what|strong="H00834"\w* \w she had gleaned|strong="H03950"\w*. \w And she brought out|strong="H03318"\w* \w what|strong="H00834"\w* \w she had saved|strong="H03498"\w* \w from her meal|strong="H07648"\w* \w and gave it|strong="H05414"\w* to [Naomi] \w -|strong="H00853"\w*.
