\p \v 14 \w So she lay down|strong="H07901"\w* \w at his feet|strong="H04772"\w* \w until|strong="H05704"\w* \w morning|strong="H01242"\w*, \w but she got up|strong="H06965"\w* \w before|strong="H02958"\w* \w anyone|strong="H00376"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w else|strong="H07453"\w* \w could recognize her|strong="H05234"\w*.
\p \w Then Boaz said|strong="H00559"\w*, “\w Do not|strong="H00408"\w* \w let it be known|strong="H03045"\w* \w that|strong="H03588"\w* \w a woman|strong="H00802"\w* \w came|strong="H00935"\w* \w to the threshing floor|strong="H01637"\w*.” \v 15 \w And he told her|strong="H00559"\w*, “\w Bring|strong="H03051"\w* \w the shawl|strong="H04304"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w you are wearing|strong="H05921"\w* \w and hold|strong="H00270"\w* it out.” \w When she [did so]|strong="H00270"\w* . . ., \w he poured in|strong="H04058"\w* \w six [measures]|strong="H08337"\w* \w of barley|strong="H08184"\w*\f + \fr 3:15 \ft Possibly six seahs (two ephahs), or approximately 39.6 dry quarts or 43.8 liters (about 58 pounds or 26.3 kilograms of barley) \f* \w and placed it|strong="H07896"\w* \w on her|strong="H05921"\w*. \w Then he went|strong="H00935"\w*\f + \fr 3:15 \ft Most Hebrew manuscripts; many Hebrew manuscripts, Vulgate, and Syriac \fqa she went\f* \w into the city|strong="H05892"\w*.
\p \v 16 \w When Ruth returned|strong="H00935"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w her mother-in-law|strong="H02545"\w*, \w Naomi asked her|strong="H00559"\w*, “\w How did it go|strong="H04310"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00859"\w*, \w my daughter|strong="H01323"\w*?”
\p \w Then Ruth told|strong="H05046"\w* her \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w all|strong="H03605"\w* \w that|strong="H00834"\w* \w [Boaz]|strong="H00376"\w* \w had done|strong="H06213"\w* for her. \v 17 \w And she said|strong="H00559"\w*, “\w He gave|strong="H05414"\w* me \w these|strong="H00428"\w* \w six|strong="H08337"\w* \w measures of barley|strong="H08184"\w*, \w for|strong="H03588"\w* \w he said|strong="H00559"\w*, ‘\w Do not|strong="H00408"\w* \w go back|strong="H00935"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w your mother-in-law|strong="H02545"\w* \w empty-handed|strong="H07387"\w*.’”
\p \v 18 “\w Wait|strong="H03427"\w*, \w my daughter|strong="H01323"\w*,” \w said Naomi|strong="H00559"\w*, “\w until|strong="H05704"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w you find out|strong="H03045"\w* \w how|strong="H00349"\w* \w things|strong="H01697"\w* \w go|strong="H05307"\w*, \w for|strong="H03588"\w* \w he|strong="H00376"\w* \w will not|strong="H03808"\w* \w rest|strong="H08252"\w* \w unless|strong="H03588"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00518"\w* \w he has resolved|strong="H03615"\w* \w the matter|strong="H01697"\w* \w today|strong="H03117"\w*.”
\c 4
\s1 Boaz Redeems Ruth
\p \v 1 \w Meanwhile, Boaz|strong="H01162"\w* \w went|strong="H05927"\w* \w to the gate|strong="H08179"\w* \w and sat down|strong="H03427"\w* \w there|strong="H08033"\w*. \w Soon|strong="H02009"\w* \w the kinsman-redeemer|strong="H01350"\w*\f + \fr 4:1 \ft The Hebrew word for \fqa kinsman-redeemer \ft or \fqa guardian-redeemer\ft is a legal term for the kinsman who redeems or vindicates a relative; also in verses 3, 6, 8, and 14; see Leviticus 25:25–55.\f* \w of whom [he]|strong="H01162"\w* \w had spoken|strong="H01696"\w* \w came along|strong="H05674"\w*, \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w and Boaz said|strong="H00559"\w*, “\w Come over|strong="H05493"\w* \w here|strong="H06311"\w*, \w my friend|strong="H06423"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00492"\w*, \w and sit down|strong="H03427"\w*.” \w So he went over|strong="H05493"\w* \w and sat down|strong="H03427"\w*.
\p \v 2 \w Then Boaz took|strong="H03947"\w* \w ten|strong="H06235"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00582"\w* \w of the elders|strong="H02205"\w* \w of the city|strong="H05892"\w* \w and said|strong="H00559"\w*, “\w Sit|strong="H03427"\w* \w here|strong="H06311"\w*,” \w and they did so|strong="H03427"\w*.
\p \v 3 \w And he said|strong="H00559"\w* \w to the kinsman-redeemer|strong="H01350"\w*, “\w Naomi|strong="H05281"\w*, \w who has returned|strong="H07725"\w* \w from the land|strong="H07704"\w* \w of Moab|strong="H04124"\w*, \w is selling|strong="H04376"\w* \w the piece|strong="H02513"\w* \w of land|strong="H07704"\w* \w that|strong="H00834"\w* \w belonged to our brother|strong="H00251"\w* \w Elimelech|strong="H00458"\w*. \v 4 \w I|strong="H00589"\w* \w thought|strong="H00559"\w* \w I should inform|strong="H01540"\w* \w you|strong="H00241"\w* \w that|strong="H00559"\w* \w you may buy it back|strong="H07069"\w* \w in the presence of|strong="H05048"\w* \w those seated here|strong="H03427"\w* \w and in the presence of|strong="H05048"\w* \w the elders|strong="H02205"\w* \w of my people|strong="H05971"\w*. \w If|strong="H00518"\w* \w you want to redeem it|strong="H01350"\w*, \w do so|strong="H01350"\w*. \w But if you|strong="H00518"\w*\f + \fr 4:4 \ft Many Hebrew manuscripts, LXX, Vulgate, and Syriac; most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa he\f* \w will not|strong="H03808"\w* \w redeem [it]|strong="H01350"\w*, \w tell|strong="H05046"\w* me \w so I may know|strong="H03045"\w*, \w because|strong="H03588"\w* \w [there is] no one|strong="H00369"\w* \w but you|strong="H02108"\w* \w to redeem [it]|strong="H01350"\w*, \w and I [am]|strong="H00595"\w* \w next after you|strong="H00310"\w*.”
\p “\w I|strong="H00595"\w* \w will redeem [it]|strong="H01350"\w*,” \w he replied|strong="H00559"\w*.
\p \v 5 \w Then Boaz|strong="H01162"\w* \w said|strong="H00559"\w*, “\w On the day|strong="H03117"\w* \w you buy|strong="H07069"\w* \w the land|strong="H07704"\w* \w from|strong="H03027"\w* \w Naomi|strong="H05281"\w* \w and also from|strong="H00854"\w* \w Ruth|strong="H07327"\w* \w the Moabitess|strong="H04125"\w*, \w you must also acquire|strong="H07069"\w* \w the widow|strong="H00802"\w* \w of the deceased|strong="H04191"\w* \w in order to raise|strong="H06965"\w* \w up the name|strong="H08034"\w* \w of the deceased|strong="H04191"\w* \w on|strong="H05921"\w* \w his inheritance|strong="H05159"\w*.”
\p \v 6 \w The kinsman-redeemer|strong="H01350"\w* \w replied|strong="H00559"\w*, “\w I cannot|strong="H03808"\w* \w . . .|strong="H03201"\w* \w redeem it|strong="H01350"\w* myself, \w or|strong="H06435"\w* \w I would jeopardize|strong="H07843"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w my own inheritance|strong="H05159"\w*. \w Take my right of redemption|strong="H01353"\w* \w . . .|strong="H01350"\w* . . . \w . . .|strong="H00859"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w*, \w because|strong="H03588"\w* \w I cannot|strong="H03808"\w* \w . . .|strong="H03201"\w* \w redeem it|strong="H01350"\w*.”
\p \v 7 \w Now|strong="H02063"\w* \w in former times|strong="H06440"\w* \w in Israel|strong="H03478"\w*, \w concerning|strong="H05921"\w* \w the redemption|strong="H01353"\w* \w . . .|strong="H05921"\w* \w or exchange of property|strong="H08545"\w*, \w to make any|strong="H03605"\w* \w matter|strong="H01697"\w* \w legally binding|strong="H06965"\w* \w a man|strong="H00376"\w* \w would remove|strong="H08025"\w* \w his sandal|strong="H05275"\w* \w and give it|strong="H05414"\w* \w to the other party|strong="H07453"\w*, \w and this [was]|strong="H02063"\w* \w a confirmation|strong="H08584"\w* \w in Israel|strong="H03478"\w*. \v 8 \w So the kinsman-redeemer|strong="H01350"\w* \w removed|strong="H08025"\w* \w his sandal|strong="H05275"\w* \w and said|strong="H00559"\w* \w to Boaz|strong="H01162"\w*, “\w Buy [it]|strong="H07069"\w* for yourself.”
\p \v 9 \w At this, Boaz|strong="H01162"\w* \w said|strong="H00559"\w* \w to the elders|strong="H02205"\w* \w and all|strong="H03605"\w* \w the people|strong="H05971"\w*, “\w You|strong="H00859"\w* \w are witnesses|strong="H05707"\w* \w today|strong="H03117"\w* \w that|strong="H03588"\w* \w I am buying|strong="H07069"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w from|strong="H03027"\w* \w Naomi|strong="H05281"\w* \w all|strong="H03605"\w* \w that|strong="H00834"\w* \w belonged to Elimelech|strong="H00458"\w*, \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w -|strong="H03605"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w Chilion|strong="H03630"\w*, \w and Mahlon|strong="H04248"\w*. \v 10 \w Moreover|strong="H01571"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w*, \w I have acquired|strong="H07069"\w* . . . \w Ruth|strong="H07327"\w* \w the Moabitess|strong="H04125"\w*, \w Mahlon’s|strong="H04248"\w* \w widow|strong="H00802"\w*, \w as my wife|strong="H00802"\w*, \w to raise up|strong="H06965"\w* \w the name|strong="H08034"\w* \w of the deceased|strong="H04191"\w* \w through|strong="H05921"\w* \w his inheritance|strong="H05159"\w*, \w so that his|strong="H04191"\w* \w name|strong="H08034"\w* \w will not|strong="H03808"\w* \w disappear|strong="H03772"\w* \w from among|strong="H05973"\w* \w his brothers|strong="H00251"\w* \w or from the gate|strong="H08179"\w* \w of his home|strong="H04725"\w*. \w You|strong="H00859"\w* \w are witnesses today|strong="H05707"\w* \w . . .|strong="H03117"\w*.”
\p \v 11 “\w We are witnesses|strong="H05707"\w*,” \w said|strong="H00559"\w* \w the elders|strong="H02205"\w* \w and all|strong="H03605"\w* \w the people|strong="H05971"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w at the gate|strong="H08179"\w*. “\w May the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w make|strong="H05414"\w* \w the woman|strong="H00802"\w* \w entering|strong="H00935"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00413"\w* \w your home|strong="H01004"\w* \w like Rachel|strong="H07354"\w* \w and Leah|strong="H03812"\w*, \w who|strong="H00834"\w* \w together built up|strong="H01129"\w* \w . . .|strong="H08147"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w the house|strong="H01004"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H03478"\w*. \w May you be|strong="H06213"\w* \w prosperous|strong="H02428"\w* \w in Ephrathah|strong="H00672"\w* \w and famous|strong="H07121"\w* \w . . .|strong="H08034"\w* \w vvv|strong="H01035"\w* \w in Bethlehem|strong="H01035"\w*. \v 12 \w And may your house|strong="H01004"\w* \w become|strong="H01961"\w* \w like the house|strong="H01004"\w* \w of Perez|strong="H06557"\w*, \w whom|strong="H00834"\w* \w Tamar|strong="H08559"\w* \w bore|strong="H03205"\w* \w to Judah|strong="H03063"\w*, \w because of|strong="H04480"\w* \w the offspring|strong="H02233"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w will give|strong="H05414"\w* you \w by|strong="H04480"\w* \w this|strong="H02063"\w* \w young woman|strong="H05291"\w*.”
\s1 Boaz Marries Ruth
\p \v 13 \w So Boaz|strong="H01162"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w took|strong="H03947"\w* \w Ruth|strong="H07327"\w*, \w and she became|strong="H01961"\w* his \w wife|strong="H00802"\w*. \w And when he had relations with|strong="H00935"\w* \w her|strong="H00413"\w*, \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w enabled|strong="H05414"\w* her \w to conceive|strong="H02032"\w*, \w and she gave birth to|strong="H03205"\w* \w a son|strong="H01121"\w*.
